+## Hinting is chosen here, because an advance belongs to the rasteriser
+
+imgui-bundle bakes its atlas with FreeType (`io.fonts.font_loader_name` reads
+`FreeType (2.13.3; 2.13.3)` in 1.92.900), and FreeType hints unless it is told
+not to. A hinted glyph's advance is a whole pixel the hinter chose, and it is
+not the file's advance scaled to the size: measured at a 16 px height, Roboto's
+`p` is 7.66 px in the file and 8 in the atlas, and every glyph of Inconsolata
+is 7.63 in the file and 8 in the atlas. So an advance is a property of (font,
+size, hinting mode), and a layout measured from the file describes a raster
+only when that raster was baked unhinted.
+
+`Hinting` names the mode and `load_faces(hinting=...)` sets it on the faces this
+module loads and records it on the `LoadedFaces` it returns.
+`LoadedFaces.metrics()` is then the resolver that agrees with those faces:
+`advtext.style.fontlib_metrics` -- the file -- under `Hinting.NONE`, and
+`baked_metrics` -- the file for everything but the advance, the atlas for the
+advance -- under the two hinted modes. Measure, compose, ship and draw with what
+it returns and every advance the layout holds is the advance of the glyph that
+is drawn.
+
+**That is the whole of what `Hinting.NONE` buys, and it is less than it sounds.**
+`_RigidSpan.pen` puts every glyph on a whole pixel by rounding each gap, whatever
+the mode. Under a hinted mode with `metrics()` the gaps are whole pixels already,
+the rounding finds nothing to do, and a word is drawn at the width it was laid
+out at. Under `NONE` the advances are the file's and fractional, the rounding
+still happens, and a word's width moves as `docs/advance-rule.md` §4 says --
+by 10 px over a line of code at a 16 px height, where every Inconsolata gap of
+7.63 is drawn at 8. An unhinted atlas is the matched one for a renderer that
+places a glyph at a fractional pen, which the SVG backend does and this one
+was decided not to (`docs/subpixel.md` §4.2). `scripts/pen_rules.py --hinting`
+prints all of it.
+
+**The default is `Hinting.DEFAULT` and nothing calls `metrics()` for a host**, so
+a host that changes nothing gets what it had: the loader's default flags, and
+`fontlib_metrics` wherever it passes no resolver. That pairing is the mismatched
+one. It is the default because every test and photograph in this tree was taken
+under it, and which pairing should replace it is the user's decision
+(`docs/advance-rule.md` §2 has the measurements).
+`advtext.backends.imgui_draw.check_advances` reports a mismatched pair.
+
+Under a host's own `loader` this module sets nothing: `hinting` is then a
+statement about what that loader does, and `Hinting.loader_flags` is the value
+for the host's own `ImFontConfig.font_loader_flags`.
+
+What was run: `tests/test_hinting.py`, against a real atlas in a context with
+no backend, at one density. Not run: a window, a renderer backend, a
+`rasterizer_density` other than 1 (measured once by hand: at 2, a hinted
+advance is a whole *device* pixel, so half a layout pixel), and a build of Dear
+ImGui whose loader is stb_truetype, which has no hinter and ignores the flag.
+
