+class BakedFaceMetrics:
+    """
+    `FontMetrics` for one face at one size, with each advance as the atlas baked it.
+
+    The advance is `ImFontBaked.get_char_advance` at the pixel height `draw`
+    will ask for -- the same `baked_size_px` arithmetic, quantised by ImGui the
+    same way -- so it is the advance of the glyph that is drawn, at the size it
+    is drawn at, under whatever the loader did to it. Everything a raster does
+    not define is the file's: ascent, descent, x-height, coverage, ink boxes.
+
+    **A pair kern is taken to the pixel when the advance before it is on one.**
+    `_RigidSpan.pen` draws a gap at `snap_px(advance + kern)`. When the advance
+    is a whole pixel that is `advance + snap_px(kern)`, so the kern is rounded
+    on screen whatever is returned here; returning it rounded makes the width
+    the layout believes the width that is drawn, and the residue that would
+    otherwise land in the following word space is zero. When the advance is
+    fractional -- no hinting, or a density above 1 -- the kern is the file's,
+    unrounded, as `fontlib_metrics` gives it. `scripts/pen_rules.py --hinting`
+    measures both.
+
+    A codepoint the loaded face has no glyph for, and every codepoint when no
+    face is loaded for the role, takes the file's advance: there is no raster
+    to ask, and `draw` counts such a glyph as missing.
+
+    The numbers are copied out of the `ImFontBaked` as floats and it is not
+    held: ImGui discards a baked size nothing has drawn with for a while.
+    Needs a current ImGui context whose backend flags carry
+    `renderer_has_textures`; needs no frame.
+    """
